From d746b5e946903a3f2ead49e79211e43a8a5fad31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Leitner-Ankerl <martin.ankerl@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:11:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] x86/cpu: Use prefetcht0 for prefetch() on 64-bit

On x86-64 the kernel does not define ARCH_HAS_PREFETCH, so prefetch()
from <linux/prefetch.h> is __builtin_prefetch(). x86-64 is built with
-mno-sse, and clang then drops __builtin_prefetch without a warning,
while gcc emits prefetcht0. So every prefetch() of a clang-built x86-64
kernel is gone: defconfig with zram has 10 prefetcht0 with clang 22.1.8,
all of them inline assembly, and 845 with gcc 16.2.1.

Use prefetcht0 in inline assembly on x86-64. Not the alternative that
32-bit has: it patches in prefetchnta on every CPU with SSE, which would
turn the prefetcht0 of gcc builds into a non-temporal prefetch.

With this, clang's vmlinux has 89 prefetcht0 and gcc's still 845. Most of
gcc's are in lib/zstd, which calls __builtin_prefetch directly and stays
without prefetches in clang builds.

Measured with a zram backend that prefetches the compressed data with
prefetch() before it decompresses a page, clang 22.1.8, in a VM pinned
to one CPU of a Ryzen 9 7950X at 4.5 GHz, 20000 pages swapped out and
faulted back in, means per page, three boots each:

                      decompression    whole swap-in
  without this patch  2086..2155 ns    3887..3950 ns
  with this patch     1978..1988 ns    3761..3775 ns

lz4, which does not prefetch, swaps in the same in both, 3158..3190 ns
and 3170..3181 ns.

Signed-off-by: Martin Leitner-Ankerl <martin.ankerl@gmail.com>
---
 arch/x86/include/asm/processor.h | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/include/asm/processor.h b/arch/x86/include/asm/processor.h
index ec9db0dfa0df..a3162ae05cd6 100644
--- a/arch/x86/include/asm/processor.h
+++ b/arch/x86/include/asm/processor.h
@@ -624,15 +624,25 @@ extern int			bootloader_version;
 extern char			ignore_fpu_irq;
 
 #define HAVE_ARCH_PICK_MMAP_LAYOUT 1
+#define ARCH_HAS_PREFETCH
 #define ARCH_HAS_PREFETCHW
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_X86_32
 # define BASE_PREFETCH		""
-# define ARCH_HAS_PREFETCH
 #else
 # define BASE_PREFETCH		"prefetcht0 %1"
 #endif
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_X86_64
+/*
+ * Every x86-64 CPU has prefetcht0. Not __builtin_prefetch(): the kernel
+ * builds with -mno-sse, and clang then drops the builtin without a warning.
+ */
+static inline void prefetch(const void *x)
+{
+	asm("prefetcht0 %0" : : "m" (*(const char *)x));
+}
+#else
 /*
  * Prefetch instructions for Pentium III (+) and AMD Athlon (+)
  *
@@ -645,6 +655,7 @@ static inline void prefetch(const void *x)
 			  X86_FEATURE_XMM,
 			  "m" (*(const char *)x));
 }
+#endif
 
 /*
  * 3dnow prefetch to get an exclusive cache line.
-- 
2.56.0

